\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Must every smooth function $u:R^{10}\to R$ with everywhere positive-definite Hessian, satisfying $\Sigma _ij$ $U^ij$ $\partial _ij(det$ $D^{2}u)^{-11/12}=0$ and $U=det(D^{2}u)(D^{2}u)^{-1}$, be a quadratic polynomial plus an affine term?

\subsection{Short English statement}
Must every smooth function $u:R^{10}\to R$ with everywhere positive-definite Hessian, satisfying $\Sigma _ij$ $U^ij$ $\partial _ij(det$ $D^{2}u)^{-11/12}=0$ and $U=det(D^{2}u)(D^{2}u)^{-1}$, be a quadratic polynomial plus an affine term?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
